            <div xml:id="d459">

                <pb facs="0828" n="708" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg708"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4467</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Warren</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-26"><hi rendition="#italic">May 26,
                        1922</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received June 15.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 227</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    statement handed to me on May 16th by Count Uchida, the Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs, outlining the attitude assumed by the Japanese Government with respect
                    to the factional disturbances now taking place in North <pb facs="0829" n="709"
                        xml:id="pg709"/> China. This statement was not telegraphed to the
                    Department, as the Embassy was assured by the local agency of the Associated
                    Press that it would be telegraphed in its entirety to the United States.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles B. Warren</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d459-a1.xml" xpointer="d459-a1"/>
            </div>
